::id(doc-cfgDocRf)

=[ Configuration Reference ]

Generated by `tomet spec config` from Rust configuration definitions in `crates/tomet-config/`. Do not edit it: change the doc comments there and run the command again.

Authoritative reference of all configurable settings supported in `default.config.tmt` and in a document's own declarations, such as `::format(...)` and `::field(...)`.

==[ format ]

Formatting and printer rule configuration.

- `paragraph.separator` (string): How a paragraph is separated from the block after it (`blank` or `semicolon`). Applies between paragraphs and the elements, holes and interpolations that stand like one; a heading, a list or a code block keeps the blank line it has. Unset, the formatter leaves each separator as written and the printer, which has none to keep, writes a blank line.
- `map.align_values` (bool, default: `false`): Align the values of consecutive `key: value` lines of a `(...)` group written over several lines, the colon staying on the key (`meta:    {...}` over `heading: {...}`). A blank line, a comment, or an entry whose value runs over several lines ends a run. Off, each line keeps the spacing it has.
- `map.max_key_width` (int, default: `20`): Widest key, in display columns, that `map.align_values` pads the others to. A longer key is written `key: value` and neither widens the others nor ends the run.
- `heading.space_inside_brackets` (bool, default: `false`): Space inside brackets for headings (`=[ title ]` vs `=[title]`).
- `link.no_space` (bool, default: `false`): Omit spaces around link content (`@[content]` vs `@ [content]`). Aliases: `wikilink.no_space`.
- `link.group_order` (string, default: `()[]`): Delimiter group order for links (`()[]` vs `[]()`). Aliases: `link.order`, `wikilink.group_order`, `wikilink.order`.
- `element.group_order` (string, default: `args_first`): Default delimiter group order for all elements. Aliases: `element.order`, `group_order`.
- `callout.style.content` (string): Callout box content style (e.g. "block", "quote").
- `list.multiline.style.content` (string): Multiline list item content style (e.g. "box", "bullet").
- `table.adjust_width` (string | bool, default: `auto`): Table column width alignment behavior ("auto", "true", "false").
- `table.max_col_width` (int, default: `20`): Maximum column width threshold for table alignment.
- `table.align` (string): Default text alignment in table cells ("left", "center", "right").

==[ meta ]

Document metadata formatting and schema rules.

- `meta.always_newline` (bool, default: `false`): Always write metadata keys on separate newlines.
- `meta.<field>.type` (string): Expected semantic data type of the metadata field (e.g. `string`, `list`, `datetime`).
- `meta.<field>.format` (string): Datetime or string format pattern (e.g. `rfc3339`).
- `meta.<field>.offset` (string): Fixed timezone offset string (e.g. `+09:00`).
- `meta.<field>.always_newline` (bool, default: `false`): Force trailing newline formatting for this field in `::meta(...)`.
- `meta.<field>.length` (int): Fixed or maximum list length.
- `meta.<field>.prefix` (string): Static string prefix.
- `meta.<field>.force` (bool): Force presence validation.
- `meta.<field>.overwrite` (bool): Allow overwriting during migrations.

==[ workspace ]

Workspace-level configuration for vault indexing and file discovery.

- `workspace.ignore` (list(string)): Paths that are not part of this vault (neither swept nor resolvable). Aliases: `ignore.files`.
- `workspace.unswept` (list(string)): Paths that are in the vault and left alone (e.g. `tests/fixtures` frozen test corpus).
- `workspace.folder.entry` (string, default: `self.tmt`): The file name of a Folder's entry file: the file in a directory whose leading `::` declarations are that Folder's own settings, laid over the vault config for the Folder and below. One name for the whole vault, so only the vault config sets it. A bare file name: not empty, no path separator, not `.` or `..`.

==[ registry ]

Blueprint, vocabulary and dictionary file registry declarations.

- `blueprints` (list(string)): Blueprint files this vault declares, as paths relative to the config's directory.
- `vocabularies` (list(string)): Vocabulary files this vault declares, each naming itself with `::vocabulary.ns()`.
- `dictionaries` (list(string)): Dictionary files this vault declares, each naming itself with `::dictionary(name)`.
